+## v0.3 network command center
+
+- Optional UnderWeb network manifest at `https://underweb.cloud/api/uwx/manifest`, with local cached fallback when the website feed is unavailable.
+- Connected Accounts panel for the existing UnderWeb account, verified VRChat identity, and Discord link.
+- Role-aware network directory for Staff, Creators, Partners, creator types, and badges.
+- Auto Invite role presets for UnderWeb Staff, Creators, and Partners in addition to v0.2 friend audiences.
+- Event Mode for live/upcoming UnderWeb events, instance metadata, staff/talent counts, and event links.
+- Network Radar filters and role summaries.
+- Friend profile quick-view with UnderWeb roles and direct public-profile access when linked.
+- Persistent notification rules and release-channel/update status.
+
+The network integration is deliberately tolerant of the website endpoint not existing yet: UWX remains usable as a VRCX-derived client, displays the network as offline/cached, and automatically activates the connected features once the manifest endpoint is deployed.
+
 ## Important internal compatibility note
 
 The native .NET assembly, namespaces, database filenames, IPC class names, and many internal `VRCX_*` config keys intentionally remain unchanged in this milestone. They are implementation details relied on by the Electron/.NET bridge. User-facing branding can change independently without destabilizing that bridge.
